A||||4||ggarsk||Oil bath aircleaner||||1||
Z||000000||ggarsk||06-30-2000||01:40 PM||||It seems my '84 has a oil bath aircleaner. Oil is being sucked out thru the crankacse breather filter into my air filter. I've changed the PCV valve,breather filter. It still does it. Just put a new EGR valve. Does anybody have an idea what is causing this. I'm at my wits end. Atleast I know that no dirt is getting past my air filter.||||reg||1
Z||000001||deceler8||06-30-2000||08:15 PM||||Hope you're not being overwhelmed by blowby from a worn out engine.<P>Be sure there's vacuum going to the PCV valve itself (take it out and place your finger against it at idle...should feel a vacuum).<P>Didn't put the valve in backwards, did you ?<P>And be sure all the grommets on your valve cover are tight and that your gasket isn't leaking. Really sounds like blowby, though.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Taijiguy||06-30-2000||08:49 PM||||A pretty solid indicator of bad rings is oil leaks around the pan, pressure forcing oil out through the seals. <p>[This message has been edited by Taijiguy (edited 06-30-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||ka4nkf||07-01-2000||07:16 AM||||When I had my 84 It did the same thing. I was using a AC air filter and come to find out they are impregnated with oil. I switched to fram and no more problem.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Linx||07-02-2000||02:31 PM||||Time for a compression check;  oil in the intake is blowby from bad rings.||||reg||1
